{"base_rate":0.4848084544253633,"brier":0.1927586525759577,"bss":0.22825296513658933,"bss_hi":0.3066206682002112,"bss_lo":0.1269947230413694,"chart":{"base":[481.1,183.3],"fp":[503.8,240.1],"lead":"62,255.7 272,233.9 482,192.8 692,125.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.23 — higher than 33% of cities","fp":"low end +18pp, high end +13pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 55% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 21%; promised 93% → rained 80%"},"rel":"77.9,373.3 307.4,297.2 648.7,119.5"},"country":"FR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13256274768824303,"ess":418.7371735260061,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Lille</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Lille rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>86%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>18%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nLILLE-LESQUIN, 7.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.23, ranked 145 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(97&ndash;171) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>214</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>89</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Lille</b> <span class=\"muted\">France</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;48% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 48% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.23</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>97&ndash;171\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Lille &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Lille\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.257196261682246,376.89719626168227 85.32561797752808,332.92134831460675 144.20378378378376,254.1081081081081 245.62,150.36363636363637 333.3281578947368,65.89473684210526 405.886872246696,19.60352422907488 405.886872246696,30.82819383259914 333.3281578947368,132.94736842105263 245.62,226.11818181818182 144.20378378378376,327.8918918918919 85.32561797752808,373.82022471910113 59.257196261682246,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"205.52972258916776\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"205.52972258916776\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.257196261682246,315.66355140186914 85.32561797752808,275.6629213483146 144.20378378378376,283.6216216216216 245.62,197.63636363636365 333.3281578947368,156.89473684210526 405.886872246696,67.70925110132157\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 214 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.257196261682246\" cy=\"315.66355140186914\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 89 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"85.32561797752808\" cy=\"275.6629213483146\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 24%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"144.20378378378376\" cy=\"283.6216216216216\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 53%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"245.62\" cy=\"197.63636363636365\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"333.3281578947368\" cy=\"156.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 227 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"405.886872246696\" cy=\"67.70925110132157\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(48%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Lille the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.26) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.13).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'>0.129</td><td class='num'>12.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.178</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.215</td><td class='num'>13.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>0.258</td><td class='num'>13.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":50.63391,"lon":3.05512,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Lille","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0035514018691588786,"n":214,"obs":0.1822429906542056,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14400000000000035,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.07719101123595505,"n":89,"obs":0.29213483146067415,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.14400000000000035,"mean":0.2435135135135135,"n":74,"obs":0.2702702702702703,"sig":false},{"hi":0.6760000000000008,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.53,"n":77,"obs":0.5064935064935064,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8620000000000004,"lo":0.6760000000000008,"mean":0.7777631578947368,"n":76,"obs":0.618421052631579,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.8620000000000004,"mean":0.9827312775330396,"n":227,"obs":0.8634361233480177,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":7.7,"provisional":false,"rank":145,"rank_hi":171.0,"rank_lo":96.95,"reliability":0.021401205333859214,"resolution":0.07957226061813877,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"lille","station":"LILLE-LESQUIN","timezone":"Europe/Paris"}